sks is the  takeaway points if you want to not  compromise the quality of your product  and the viability of the cells so in  summary we found that using the quantum  automated system instead of using the  manual multi layer flask based protocols  resulted in almost a 50% reduction in  the cost of reagents and consumables  needed to produce  100 doses of MSDS to run this  hypothetical clinical trial and using  the automated method resulted and about  a 17% decrease in the amount of actual  time needed to grow out this many cells  and using the automated method resulted  in an 82% reduction in the number of  hours needed to be expended by the  technologist in order to do all this  work and only require the effort of one  technologist versus two or more  technologists to do all the manual tasks  efficiently and we've concluded that we  are able to produce large quantities of  bone marrow Mozingo stem cells for  clinical use using the automated quantum  system and that it requires  significantly less cost time and effort  on our part to do this over the manual  method using certain multi-layer flasks  and that indeed is the method the  platform that we have gone with for all  of our future manufacturing needs  you  excellent presentation Athena thanks for  bringing that information to us we now  welcome Brent rice PhD from the sole  processing team at Tru mobi CT was a  collaborator with Athena and now joins  us to answer your questions before we  get started with the Q&amp;A sessions here's  a quick reminder about how to reach us  today questions can be sent they have a  green Q&amp;A button at the lower left of  the presentation window we'll get to as  many as we can our first question is did  you do a comparability study between  sell products grown in a flask and cells  grown in the bioreactor yes indeed  Athena did perform a comparability study  according to their critical quality  attributes so they're indications of  identity purity potency and safety and  they 